;; Reviewed 2026-10-09 by the user (written by Claude, from the
;; design, the MACRO manual and the VAX's listing). Why this is
;; right:
;; - MemoryLayout's layout (section 4): Point is x at 0, y at 2, 4 bytes,
;;   aligned to a word. Shape is kind at 0, corner at 2, size at 8 (a
;;   longword), tags at 12, big at 16: 24 bytes, aligned to a longword;
;;   shapes[k] is 24k bytes on.
;; - A field is a displacement: p.y is P+2, s.corner.y S+4. Through a VAR
;;   parameter, @4(AP), the record's address is moved to a register first,
;;   MOVL 4(AP), Rn, the field then 2(Rn) (Move, line 28), since @4(AP)
;;   has no displacement; pt.x, at 0, is @4(AP) itself.
;; - shapes[i] is checked, scaled by MULL2 #24 and made an address by
;;   MOVAB SHAPES[R0], R0; its fields are displacements from R0, and
;;   shapes[i].tags[n] is 12(R0)[R1].
;; - A whole record is copied by MOVC3 of its size (r := p, s.corner :=
;;   p, shapes[2] := s, and in Local).
;; - A record value parameter is passed by its address (MOVAB S, or
;;   MOVAB (R0) for an element) and copied to the callee's frame on entry,
;;   after the locals are cleared: Area's MOVC3 #24, @4(AP), -24(FP), so
;;   that sh.size := ... changes only the copy. Area's and Local's masks
;;   save R2-R5 for MOVC3.
;; - A read-only one (Peek's sh-) is not copied: its address is used, as
;;   a VAR parameter's (section 7). First's VAR sh is its address, with no
;;   type tag until Phase 16.
;; - Local's frame: a at -4, b at -8, t, aligned to a longword, at -32,
;;   c at -33, rounded to 36 bytes, cleared by CLRQ and CLRL.
;; - POC_TRAP, outside the module, is named in general mode, G^ (section
;;   7, decided with the user 2026-10-06), which the linker makes
;;   relative or absolute as the symbol is relocatable or absolute (MACRO
;;   5.2.5), so that a routine in a shareable image is reached too
;;   ("always use general addressing mode for any external reference",
;;   Linker 4.2).
;; - Step 8 (decided 2026-10-08) adds the module's key, POC_K1_ and its
;;   .sym's key, a global symbol its importers declare .EXTERNAL, and, as
;;   it is the program's main module, the program's start,
;;   VAXRECORDS_MAIN, which calls the initializer, returns SS$_NORMAL and
;;   is named by .END.
;; - Phase 16 step 3 (section 14, item 4) adds Point's and Shape's type
;;   descriptors, as every record type declared at the module's level
;;   gets, in POC_CONST: the size (4 and 24, as above), extension level
;;   0, no pointers, and the descriptor's own address as its base type at
;;   level 0. They are global, label::, though neither type is exported:
;;   a pointer type that is exported may be bound to a record type that
;;   is not, and its importers' NEW names the record's descriptor.
